From blackwel at fas.harvard.edu  Wed Feb 20 09:27:57 2008
From: blackwel at fas.harvard.edu (Matt Blackwell)
Date: Wed, 20 Feb 2008 09:27:57 -0500
Subject: [amelia] Are identification variables used in the MI calculations or not?
In-Reply-To: <47BC37FB.4070101@ethz.ch>
References: <47BC37FB.4070101@ethz.ch>
Message-ID: <839691710802200627q1925e95dlcc180c813c16c54@mail.gmail.com>

Hello Marcus,

The identification vars are removed from the dataset before the
algorithm is run and returned to their rightful columns once the
algorithm has finished. Thus, (b) is the correct answer. You would get
the same results from Amelia if you sent it your data with those ID
columns removed.

good luck,
matt.

